<title>FRANCE: Ecco H1 pretax profit up 52.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Ecco H1 pretax profit up 52.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>Net attrib profit before tax and exployee profit share</p>
<p>							 550  up  52.4 pct</p>
<p>Pre-tax pre exceptional</p>
<p>	- human resources			  443  up  15.8 pct</p>
<p>	- Group Ecco				 481  vs  10.1 pct</p>
<p>   Exceptionals			  gain   155  No comparison</p>
<p>Turnover</p>
<p>	- human resources			9.005  up 7.9 pct</p>
<p>	- Group Ecco			    10.466  up 8.7 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - The Ecco group made up of employment services, security and cleaning services, said the results did not take into account creation of the new group Adecco. The results include an exceptional gain of 155 million francs reflecting from sale of shares linked with its merger with Swiss temporary employment firm Adia. It added that in line with its previous announcement, its cleaning and security services would soon be sold. Adia is merging with Ecco to create a new temporary job firm Adecco.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
